<style>
  /* One row of options, not four stacked blocks. align-items:start so opening a
     <details> grows only its own card instead of stretching every sibling. */
  .apimcp-bar { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.75rem; margin: 1rem 0 0; }
  /* flex over a fixed 4-column grid: two of the four cards are conditional, and a
     grid would leave a hole in the row on the sections that render three or two. */
  .apimcp-card { flex: 1 1 220px; min-width: 0; background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e3e7ee; border-left: 3px solid var(--apimcp-accent, #6c757d); border-radius: 10px; padding: 0.9rem 1rem; }
  .apimcp-card h4 { font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1a1a2e; margin: 0 0 0.35rem; }
  .apimcp-card p { font-size: 0.78rem; line-height: 1.4; color: #6c757d; margin: 0; }
  .apimcp-card p + p, .apimcp-card > * + p { margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  .apimcp-card code { font-size: 0.72rem; word-break: break-all; }
  .apimcp-card summary { font-size: 0.78rem; color: #0d6efd; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; }
  .apimcp-card summary:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .apimcp-card details { margin-top: 0.15rem; }
  .apimcp-card ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0.5rem 0 0; font-size: 0.78rem; }
  .apimcp-card ul li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .apimcp-card ul li span { display: block; color: #6c757d; }
  .apimcp-card pre { background: #f6f8fa; border: 1px solid #e3e7ee; border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.5rem; margin: 0; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all; }
  .apimcp-curl { margin-top: 0.6rem; }
  .apimcp-curl .apimcp-label { display: block; font-size: 0.72rem; color: #6c757d; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  .apimcp-link { display: inline-block; margin-top: 0.55rem; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 600; color: #0d6efd; text-decoration: none; }
  .apimcp-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  /* Three auth providers side by side keeps this card the same height as the
     others; stacked buttons were what made the row ragged. */
  .apimcp-auth { display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; margin-top: 0.15rem; }
  .apimcp-auth a { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.3rem; padding: 0.35rem 0.4rem; border: 1px solid #d7dce5; border-radius: 6px; background: #fff; color: #4a5568; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .apimcp-auth a:hover { border-color: #0d6efd; color: #0d6efd; }
  .apimcp-auth svg { flex: none; }
  @media (max-width: 575.98px) { .apimcp-card { flex-basis: 100%; } }
</style>



<h2 class="section-anchor" id="api-mcp"><a href="#api-mcp">Work with this as data</a></h2>
<p class="section-blurb">
  Every provider here is available over the APIs.io API and to AI agents over MCP.</p>

<div class="apimcp-bar">

  <div class="apimcp-card" style="--apimcp-accent: #3098d8;">
    <h4>MCP server</h4>
    <p>One button, every client — Claude, Cursor, VS Code and the rest.</p>
    <script src="https://install.apicommons.org/button.js" async></script>
    <mcp-install-button server="https://apis.io/server.json" label="Install the MCP server" color="#3098d8"></mcp-install-button>
    <p><code>https://apis.io/mcp</code></p>
  </div>
  <div class="apimcp-card" style="--apimcp-accent: #6d28d9;">
    <h4>Tools for providers</h4>
    <details>
      <summary>9 MCP tools reach this</summary>
      <ul>
        <li><code>find_providers</code><span>Browse and filter every provider in the catalog.</span></li>
        <li><code>get_provider_artifacts</code><span>Every artifact this provider publishes, grouped by type.</span></li>
        <li><code>get_provider_operations</code><span>Every operation across all of their OpenAPIs — one call instead of parsing every spec.</span></li>
        <li><code>get_provider_tools</code><span>Every MCP tool they ship, with the operation each wraps.</span></li>
        <li><code>get_provider_evidence</code><span>How each part of their score was established. Free — the basis for a claim should not sit behind it.</span></li>
        <li><code>get_provider_rating</code><span>PRO — composite, band, trend and facet scores.</span></li>
        <li><code>apis_io_search</code><span>START HERE — APIs, providers and tags for one query, each with its total.</span></li>
        <li><code>resolve</code><span>Turn a domain, URL or GitHub org into the provider it belongs to.</span></li>
        <li><code>find_cohorts</code><span>Every scored population of providers in the catalog.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </details>
    <a href="https://apis.io/developer/mcp-server/" class="apimcp-link">All 92 tools &rarr;</a>
  </div>
  <div class="apimcp-card" style="--apimcp-accent: #198754;">
    <h4>Call it yourself</h4>
    <details>
      <summary>curl for this page</summary>
      <div class="apimcp-curl">
        <span class="apimcp-label">This provider</span>
        <pre><code>curl "https://apis.io/api/v1/providers/attestedmemory-net"</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="apimcp-curl">
        <span class="apimcp-label">All providers</span>
        <pre><code>curl "https://apis.io/api/v1/providers?limit=25"</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="apimcp-curl">
        <span class="apimcp-label">Every operation they expose</span>
        <pre><code>curl "https://apis.io/api/v1/providers/attestedmemory-net/operations?limit=25"</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="apimcp-curl">
        <span class="apimcp-label">How their score was established</span>
        <pre><code>curl "https://apis.io/api/v1/providers/attestedmemory-net/evidence"</code></pre>
      </div>
    </details>
    <script>
      /* roadmap#1080: paid examples carry only a path, so crawlers cannot lift a URL from the
         page text and fetch it unkeyed. Assembled here when the reader opens the card. */
      document.querySelectorAll('.apimcp-card details').forEach(function (d) {
        d.addEventListener('toggle', function () {
          d.querySelectorAll('code.apimcp-paid:empty').forEach(function (el) {
            el.textContent = 'curl "' + 'https://apis.io/api/v1/' + el.getAttribute('data-p') + '" \\\n  -H "X-API-Key: $APIS_IO_KEY"';
          });
        }, { once: true });
      });
    </script>
    <p>Calls without <code>X-API-Key</code> need no key. Calls with it need a paid plan &mdash; <a href="https://apis.io/developer/account/?access=1">get a key</a>.</p>
  </div><div class="apimcp-card" style="--apimcp-accent: #6c757d;">
    <h4>Get an API key</h4>
    <!-- roadmap#272 — this said "no email required". The intent was "no form to fill in";
         what it told a data subject AT THE MOMENT OF COLLECTION was that no email is
         collected. The callback stores one on every account it creates (auth/index.mjs)
         and indexes it in the EmailIndex GSI, and a verified email is what joins a second
         provider to an existing account. The copy has to say what the code does. -->
    <p>Free tier, no form to fill in. Signing in shares your email address with us — we
      store it to create your key and to recognise you if you sign in with another
      provider. See our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and
      <a href="/terms/">Terms</a>.</p>
    <div class="apimcp-auth">
      <a href="https://apis.io/api/v1/auth/login?provider=github">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27s1.36.09 2 .27c1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.01 8.01 0 0 0 16 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8Z"/></svg>
        <span>GitHub</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://apis.io/api/v1/auth/login?provider=google">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 18 18" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="#4285F4" d="M17.64 9.2c0-.64-.06-1.25-.16-1.84H9v3.48h4.84a4.14 4.14 0 0 1-1.8 2.72v2.26h2.92c1.7-1.57 2.68-3.88 2.68-6.62Z"/><path fill="#34A853" d="M9 18c2.43 0 4.47-.8 5.96-2.18l-2.92-2.26c-.81.54-1.84.86-3.04.86-2.34 0-4.32-1.58-5.03-3.7H.96v2.33A9 9 0 0 0 9 18Z"/><path fill="#FBBC05" d="M3.97 10.72a5.41 5.41 0 0 1 0-3.44V4.95H.96a9 9 0 0 0 0 8.1l3.01-2.33Z"/><path fill="#EA4335" d="M9 3.58c1.32 0 2.5.45 3.44 1.35l2.58-2.58C13.46.89 11.43 0 9 0A9 9 0 0 0 .96 4.95l3.01 2.33C4.68 5.16 6.66 3.58 9 3.58Z"/></svg>
        <span>Google</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://apis.io/api/v1/auth/login?provider=linkedin">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="#0A66C2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20.45 20.45h-3.56v-5.57c0-1.33-.03-3.04-1.85-3.04-1.85 0-2.14 1.45-2.14 2.94v5.67H9.35V9h3.41v1.56h.05c.48-.9 1.63-1.85 3.36-1.85 3.6 0 4.27 2.37 4.27 5.45v6.29ZM5.34 7.43a2.06 2.06 0 1 1 0-4.13 2.06 2.06 0 0 1 0 4.13ZM7.12 20.45H3.55V9h3.57v11.45ZM22.22 0H1.77C.79 0 0 .77 0 1.72v20.56C0 23.23.79 24 1.77 24h20.45c.98 0 1.78-.77 1.78-1.72V1.72C24 .77 23.2 0 22.22 0Z"/></svg>
        <span>LinkedIn</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p>A second provider on the same verified email joins the account you already have.</p>
  </div>

</div>

